Contoso Ltd. operates an Azure Storage account (contosouploads) that receives files uploaded by external partners through a web application. The security team wants to configure Microsoft Defender for Storage so that every file is automatically scanned for malicious content immediately after it is uploaded, and any malicious file triggers a security alert in Microsoft Defender for Cloud. The team also wants to set a monthly capacity limit (in GB) on how much data is scanned to control costs.

Which Defender for Storage capability should you configure to meet these requirements?
正解
Malware Scanning (on-upload)
説明
This answer is correct. Malware Scanning in Defender for Storage uses the Microsoft Defender Antimalware engine to scan blobs near real-time as they are uploaded, generates security alerts for detected malware, and allows administrators to configure a monthly capacity (GB) limit for scanning to manage costs.
Sensitive Data Threat Detection
説明
