回答は不正解です
Activity Monitoring
説明
This answer is incorrect. Activity Monitoring analyzes control-plane and data-plane operations (such as unusual access patterns, permission changes, or exfiltration attempts) to detect anomalous behavior, but it does not perform content-level malware scanning of uploaded files.
Microsoft Defender for Cloud regulatory compliance assessments
説明
This answer is incorrect. Regulatory compliance assessments in Microsoft Defender for Cloud evaluate resources against compliance standards and benchmarks; they are unrelated to malware detection or file scanning capabilities.
全体的な説明
Malware Scanning is the specific Defender for Storage feature that scans uploaded blobs using the Microsoft Defender Antimalware engine, raises alerts on detection, and supports configuring a monthly GB scanning cap for cost control—directly matching all the stated requirements. The other options address different threat scenarios (sensitive data exposure, anomalous activity, or compliance) and do not perform malware scanning.
