- Calls to the Logic App must be authenticated using the partner's Microsoft Entra ID app registration.
- The Logic App must validate that the caller presents a valid OAuth bearer token issued by Microsoft Entra ID before the workflow runs.
- The built-in SAS-based trigger URL should no longer be sufficient on its own to invoke the workflow.

You need to configure the Logic App to meet these requirements with the least administrative effort.

What should you do?
Configure an IP-based access restriction on the Logic App's Access control (CORS/IP) settings to allow only the partner's public IP range.
説明
This answer is incorrect. IP restrictions limit which network locations can reach the Logic App endpoint, but they do not validate identity or require an OAuth token, so they do not meet the requirement to authenticate the caller via Microsoft Entra ID.
Enable a system-assigned managed identity on the Logic App and grant it the Logic App Contributor role.
説明
This answer is incorrect. A system-assigned managed identity is used so the Logic App can authenticate to other Azure resources when making outbound calls; it does not validate inbound callers or enforce authentication on the Request trigger itself.
Create an API connection to Microsoft Entra ID and use it as an action immediately after the Request trigger to validate the caller's token.
説明
This answer is incorrect. There is no action that validates an inbound bearer token this way, and adding an action after the trigger would not prevent unauthenticated requests from reaching and executing the trigger itself; authentication must be enforced on the trigger before the run starts.
回答は正解です
On the Request trigger, configure Azure Active Directory Open Authentication (Microsoft Entra ID authentication) and specify the allowed tenant, audience, and issuer values.
説明
This answer is correct. Logic Apps (Consumption) support configuring Microsoft Entra ID authentication directly on the Request trigger, which requires callers to present a valid OAuth bearer token from Microsoft Entra ID and lets you restrict access by tenant, audience, and issuer, replacing reliance on the SAS-based URL alone.
全体的な説明
To require Microsoft Entra ID–based authentication for callers of an HTTP-triggered Logic App, you configure Azure Active Directory Open Authentication directly on the Request trigger, specifying the expected tenant, audience, and issuer. This ensures only requests with a valid Entra ID token are accepted, superseding reliance on the SAS-protected trigger URL alone.
