A company stores sensitive customer documents in Azure Blob Storage within a storage account named "contosodocs". The security team discovers that several blob containers have been individually configured to allow anonymous public read access, exposing sensitive data to the internet. The security team wants to ensure that no blob container in this storage account can ever be configured for anonymous public access, regardless of how individual container-level settings are configured by data owners in the future.

Which setting should the security team configure to meet this requirement?
Generate a shared access signature (SAS) token with read-only permissions for all client applications
説明
This answer is incorrect. A SAS token controls delegated access for specific clients with defined permissions and expiration, but it does nothing to prevent containers from being configured for anonymous public access. SAS tokens are a separate access mechanism unrelated to blocking public container settings.
Enable "Secure transfer required" on the storage account
説明
This answer is incorrect. "Secure transfer required" enforces the use of HTTPS (and SMB encryption) for data in transit, protecting data from interception on the network, but it has no effect on whether a container can be configured for anonymous public read access.
回答は正解です
Set "Allow Blob public access" to Disabled at the storage account level
説明
This answer is correct. The "Allow Blob public access" setting at the storage account level acts as a master switch; when disabled, it overrides any container-level anonymous access configuration, ensuring that no container can be set to allow public access even if a data owner attempts to enable it later.
Assign the Azure RBAC role "Storage Blob Data Reader" to all users who need access
説明
This answer is incorrect. Assigning Azure RBAC roles controls access for authenticated Microsoft Entra identities, but it does not prevent a container from being independently configured to allow anonymous (unauthenticated) public access, since that setting operates outside of RBAC.
全体的な説明
The storage account-level "Allow Blob public access" setting is the definitive control point for preventing anonymous public access to blob data; when disabled, it takes precedence over any individual container's public access configuration, providing a tenant/account-wide guardrail. The other options address different security concerns—data-in-transit encryption, delegated temporary access, or authenticated access control—none of which prevent public anonymous access at the container level.
