When configuring an AI Gateway in Azure API Management for Microsoft Foundry backends, the azure-openai-token-limit policy is specifically designed to parse token usage from Azure OpenAI Service responses and enforce limits per key, subscription, or other identifiers, enabling fine-grained cost and abuse control that generic call-based or network-based policies cannot provide.
